Capri's body inside BabyAI (the desktop overlay)
------------------------------------------------
`python3 -m babyai --desktop` draws Capri's character using her sprites
(capri/assets/sprites) and animation rules, driven by BabyAI's own brain. These
files are ports of, or load, Capri's work and are therefore licensed under the
PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 as well, not MIT:

  babyai/ui/capri_body.py   (clip table, idle/blink/glitch/grin/sleep/wake rules,
                             mouth shapes and typing pace, petting; ported from
                             capri/cross/Pet.cs and capri/cross/Talk.cs, including
                             her three pet lines)
  babyai/ui/sprites.py      (loads and scales her sprite strips; it writes a scaled
                             copy to ~/.cache/babyai/sprites, which is also
                             noncommercial-only and is not part of this repository)

babyai/ui/app.py and babyai/ui/persona.py are BabyAI's own (MIT), but the overlay
is built to run with Capri's sprites: using or sharing BabyAI together with them is
noncommercial only. Setting `[ui] character = "stick"` in config.toml draws a plain
stick figure instead and uses none of Capri's art. The persona prompt in
persona.py is written for BabyAI; it is not Capri's personality file.

